  (ii) mixed practice, fraction f of phi-instances; per-datum difference at n = 10^6 and its limit
      f=0.9  depth:   469005.8 bits (0.4690 per datum; binary entropy h(f) = 0.4690)   shared:  1896201.6 (1.8962 per datum)
      f=0.5  depth:  1000009.8 bits (1.0000 per datum; binary entropy h(f) = 1.0000)   shared:  1377443.5 (1.3774 per datum)
      f=0.1  depth:   469004.2 bits (0.4690 per datum; binary entropy h(f) = 0.4690)   shared:   483446.3 (0.4834 per datum)

Reading.  Fixed code: log2 R bits per instance datum, exponential posterior odds.  Learned shared code: still
linear.  Learned depth-indexed code on pure instance data: (R-1)/2 log2 n + O(1), polynomial odds.  In a mixed
practice the extra step shares its context with other rules and costs about h(f)/f bits per instance datum
(linear again).  The direction (H_sch preferred) holds under every code; the rate is a property of the code
and of the practice.
